From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AML: play HDR10+ videos as Dolby Vision

On a Dolby Vision display, convert HDR10+ dynamic metadata to a Dolby
Vision profile 8.1 RPU per frame, so the display follows the per-scene
brightness. Setting "Convert HDR10+ to Dolby Vision" (Off / CM v4.0 /
CM v2.9, default Off, Standard level) under Settings > System > CoreELEC.
It is exclusive with SDR/HDR tone mapping and "Tone map HDR to Dolby
Vision". SDR/HDR tone mapping is available again while Dolby Vision
support is disabled; if it is still set when Dolby Vision support is
enabled again, it wins over SDR/HDR to Dolby Vision.

CoreELEC options: "Disable Dolby Vision support" moves to second place,
"Disable noise reduction" defaults to on, "Override level 5 metadata to
zero" defaults to off, and DV LED mode and level 5 are greyed out while
Dolby Vision support is disabled.

Refresh brightness metadata for every converted picture so decoding
pictures out of display order does not delay a scene change. Converted
HDR10+ therefore uses no Dolby Vision temporal smoothing. Video that
already carries Dolby Vision keeps its original metadata.

On kodi 326cbc50 it is also exclusive with the new "Tone map Dolby
Vision/HDR to SDR" and "Tone map Dolby Vision to HDR" settings, and the
conversion does not arm while either is stored on.

